{"id":572,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"They pet each other with their tails as a form of greeting. Of the two, the one whose tail is fluffier is a bit more boastful."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"The way it brushes away grime with its tail can be helpful when cleaning. But its focus on spotlessness can make cleaning more of a hassle."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"When its tail has gotten dirty from self-cleaning or from cleaning its nest, Minccino spends a whole day washing its tail in clean spring water."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"A clean freak that will not allow even the slightest mess, it uses its tail like a mop to thoroughly clean any and all filth."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","White"],"text":"These Pokémon prefer a tidy habitat. They are always sweeping and dusting, using their tails as brooms."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Minccino greet each other by grooming one another thoroughly with their tails."},{"games":["Black"],"text":"They greet one another by rubbing each other with their tails, which are always kept well groomed and clean."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Cute Charm","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon may infatuate attackers that make direct contact with it."},{"name":"Technician","hidden":false,"description":"Powers up weak moves so the Pokémon can deal more damage with them."},{"name":"Skill Link","hidden":true,"description":"Maximizes the number of times multistrike moves hit."}],"eggGroups":["Field"],"genderRate":6,"hatchCounter":15,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"fast","habitat":null,"color":"Gray","shape":"Quadruped","evolution":{"id":572,"name":"Minccino","condition":null,"children":[{"id":573,"name":"Cinccino","condition":"Use Shiny Stone","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,1],[1,608],[4,270],[8,497],[12,47],[16,204],[20,129],[24,227],[28,495],[32,541],[36,321],[40,21],[44,304],[48,387]],"machine":[914,226,331,347,204,886,605,91,227,283,203,263,313,374,447,44